    DR-003 Cut-off Entry Generation Wizard Views
    =============================================

    Provides the TransientModel wizard UI for period-end cut-off entry
    generation.  Backed by the TransientModel ``account.deferred.cutoff.wizard``
    defined in ``addons/account_deferred_revenue/wizard/cutoff_wizard.py``.

    Implements DR-003 acceptance criteria (6 BDD scenarios):
      1. Single Period Generation  -> mode == 'single' posts one entry per
         schedule for all qualifying recognition lines up to cutoff_date.
      2. Preview Before Posting    -> action_preview computes move_data and
         renders the preview panel; NO account.move records are created.
      3. Batch Generation          -> mode == 'batch' processes all pending
         schedules in a single pass (consolidated by company).
      4. Partial Period Proration  -> qualifying recognition lines already
         carry their prorated amounts from the schedule computation; the
         wizard merely posts them as-is.
      5. Reversal Entry            -> mode == 'reversal' (or post_reversal=True)
         invokes action_post_with_reversal which creates a reversal move
         dated reversal_date (default: first day of next period) with
         auto_post='at_date'.
      6. Lock Date Constraints     -> @api.constrains('_check_date') enforces
         all 5 lock date types (fiscalyear, tax, hard, sale, purchase); the
         lock_date_message banner surfaces any warning to the user.

    Model: account.deferred.cutoff.wizard
      - inherits models.TransientModel (non-persistent wizard)
      - _check_company_auto = True  (enforces company consistency on all
        company-bound Many2one fields)

    Views registered here:
      1. view_deferred_cutoff_wizard_form  (wizard form with 4-mode branching)
      2. action_deferred_cutoff_wizard     (window action with binding_model_id
                                           on account.deferred.schedule)

    Referenced by:
      - views/menuitem.xml via menu item ``menu_deferred_cutoff_wizard``
        (standalone invocation path from Accounting top menu).
      - account.deferred.schedule form Actions menu via binding_model_id
        (contextual invocation path on a selected schedule).
      - models/account_deferred_schedule.py ``action_generate_cutoff`` returns
        this action populated with ``default_schedule_ids`` context.

    AAP alignment notes:
      - Uses modern Odoo 19 ``invisible="<python-expr>"`` direct attribute
        syntax (NOT the legacy ``attrs="{'invisible': [...]}"`` dict form).
      - Uses ``<odoo>`` root element (NOT the legacy ``<odoo><data>`` wrapper).
      - ``binding_model_id`` references ``model_account_deferred_schedule``,
        the auto-generated ir.model xmlid that Odoo creates for every model;
        the xmlid is derived by replacing dots with underscores and prepending
        ``model_`` (i.e. ``account.deferred.schedule`` -> ``model_account_deferred_schedule``).
      - Preview panel uses ``widget="json"`` on the ``preview_move_data`` field
        to render the computed move dicts as an inline read-only JSON payload.
      - Footer button data-hotkeys follow Odoo UX conventions: ``q`` for the
        primary confirm action, ``z`` for cancel.

    Rules compliance (AAP §0.7):
      - R-01 Module Independence: only references account.deferred.cutoff.wizard
        and account.deferred.schedule (both intra-module) plus core models
        (account.journal, res.company, res.currency). No sibling new-module
        references to account_asset_management, account_budget_management, or
        account_payment_followup.
      - R-02 No Enterprise Dependencies: no references to Enterprise modules
        (account_accountant, account_reports, account_asset, account_budget,
        account_followup, account_deferred_revenue Enterprise names).
      - R-05 No Core Field Redefinition: this file declares views for the
        net-new wizard model only; no modification of any core view.
      - R-07 No sudo() without justification: not applicable to XML files.
      - R-09 Exact Module Folder Names: file path is
        ``addons/account_deferred_revenue/views/cutoff_wizard_views.xml``.
-->
<odoo>

    <!-- =================================================================
         SECTION 1: Wizard Form View
         .................................................................
         Single form view for the TransientModel wizard; opened in a modal
         dialog (target='new') via the window action defined in SECTION 2.
         Uses Odoo 19's direct ``invisible`` attribute for all
         mode-dependent field visibility.
         ================================================================= -->
    <record id="view_deferred_cutoff_wizard_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.deferred.cutoff.wizard.form</field>
        <field name="model">account.deferred.cutoff.wizard</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form string="Generate Cut-off Entries">

                <!-- =============================================
                     Lock-date Diagnostic Banner
                     Shown only when the wizard's
                     _compute_lock_date_message has populated a
                     warning (i.e. at least one lock date is
                     violated by cutoff_date).  Non-blocking: the
                     blocking enforcement lives in @api.constrains
                     _check_date which is evaluated at post time.
                     ============================================= -->
                <div class="alert alert-warning"
                     role="alert"
                     invisible="not lock_date_message">
                    <field name="lock_date_message"
                           readonly="1"
                           nolabel="1"/>
                </div>

                <sheet>

                    <!-- =========================================
                         Mode Selection
                         Horizontal radio group for the 4 modes.
                         ========================================= -->
                    <group string="Mode">
                        <field name="mode"
                               widget="radio"
                               options="{'horizontal': true}"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- =========================================
                         Schedule Selection
                         Single Many2one vs. batch/reversal M2M.
                         schedule_id is computed (first of
                         schedule_ids) and shown in single mode
                         for a compact one-schedule picker UX.
                         schedule_ids is the source of truth,
                         populated by default_schedule_ids context
                         when the wizard is opened from a schedule.
                         ========================================= -->
                    <group string="Schedule Selection">
                        <field name="schedule_id"
                               invisible="mode != 'single'"
                               required="mode == 'single'"
                               options="{'no_create': True}"
                               domain="[('state', '=', 'confirmed')]"/>
                        <field name="schedule_ids"
                               invisible="mode not in ('batch', 'reversal')"
                               required="mode in ('batch', 'reversal')"
                               widget="many2many_tags"
                               options="{'no_create': True}"
                               domain="[('state', '=', 'confirmed')]"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- =========================================
                         Posting Configuration
                         Left column: cut-off date, journal, company.
                         Right column: reversal flag & date.
                         ========================================= -->
                    <group string="Posting Configuration">
                        <group>
                            <field name="cutoff_date"/>
                            <field name="journal_id"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"
                                   domain="[('type', '=', 'general'), ('company_id', '=', company_id)]"/>
                            <field name="company_id"
                                   groups="base.group_multi_company"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                            <field name="company_currency_id"
                                   invisible="1"/>
                        </group>
                        <group>
                            <field name="post_reversal"
                                   invisible="mode == 'reversal'"/>
                            <field name="reversal_date"
                                   invisible="not post_reversal and mode != 'reversal'"
                                   required="post_reversal or mode == 'reversal'"/>
                        </group>
                    </group>

                    <!-- =========================================
                         Preview Panel
                         Visible when the user is explicitly in
                         preview mode OR when action_preview has
                         populated preview_move_data regardless of
                         mode.  The ``json`` widget renders the
                         computed move dicts read-only so the user
                         can verify accounts, amounts, and partners
                         before committing to a post.
                         ========================================= -->
                    <notebook invisible="mode != 'preview' and not preview_move_data">
                        <page name="preview" string="Preview">
                            <field name="preview_move_data"
                                   widget="json"
                                   readonly="1"
                                   nolabel="1"/>
                        </page>
                    </notebook>

                    <!-- =========================================
                         Hidden Move Data
                         Internal buffer populated by
                         _compute_move_data; consumed by
                         action_post / action_post_with_reversal
                         to create account.move records.
                         ========================================= -->
                    <field name="move_data" invisible="1"/>
                </sheet>

                <!-- =============================================
                     Footer Buttons
                     - Preview (secondary, always visible): invokes
                       action_preview to populate preview_move_data.
                     - Post Entries (primary): invokes action_post;
                       hidden in preview and reversal modes.
                     - Post with Reversal (primary): invokes
                       action_post_with_reversal; shown when mode
                       is reversal OR user has ticked post_reversal.
                     - Cancel: standard Odoo wizard cancel.
                     ============================================= -->
                <footer>
                    <button name="action_preview"
                            type="object"
                            string="Preview"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            icon="fa-eye"/>
                    <button name="action_post"
                            type="object"
                            string="Post Entries"
                            class="btn-primary"
                            icon="fa-check"
                            invisible="mode == 'preview' or mode == 'reversal'"
                            data-hotkey="q"/>
                    <button name="action_post_with_reversal"
                            type="object"
                            string="Post with Reversal"
                            class="btn-primary"
                            icon="fa-undo"
                            invisible="mode != 'reversal' and not post_reversal"/>
                    <button special="cancel"
                            string="Cancel"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            data-hotkey="z"/>
                </footer>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- =================================================================
         SECTION 2: Window Action
         .................................................................
         Opens the wizard form in a modal (target='new').  The
         ``binding_model_id`` attribute binds this action to the
         account.deferred.schedule model so it appears under the Actions
         (gear) menu on schedule form and list views.  The same action is
         also invoked from the top-level menu item declared in menuitem.xml.

         When invoked from the schedule binding, Odoo populates
         ``active_model`` and ``active_ids`` in the context, which the
         wizard's ``default_get`` uses to pre-populate ``schedule_ids``.

         ``binding_view_types`` = 'list,form' means the action appears on
         both the schedule list view and the schedule form view.  The
         'list,form' ordering follows the Odoo 19 convention (list first,
         form second) consistent with the rest of this module's view
         declarations and with the FEATURE-001/FEATURE-002 precedent.
         ================================================================= -->
    <record id="action_deferred_cutoff_wizard" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Generate Cut-off Entries</field>
        <field name="res_model">account.deferred.cutoff.wizard</field>
        <field name="view_mode">form</field>
        <field name="target">new</field>
        <field name="view_id" ref="view_deferred_cutoff_wizard_form"/>
        <field name="binding_model_id" ref="model_account_deferred_schedule"/>
        <field name="binding_view_types">list,form</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
